Hamiltonian‑Astrophysical Genetics Simulation Engine (H‑AGSE)

Unified Energy‑Landscape Simulation Architecture

1. Executive Summary

The Hamiltonian‑Astrophysical Genetics Simulation Engine (H‑AGSE) is a unified computational framework designed to model astrophysical structures, genetic regulatory networks, and molecular dynamics under a single Hamiltonian energy formulation. The system integrates multi‑scale datasets, applies high‑performance computational methods, and enforces strict encryption standards to ensure secure scientific processing. H‑AGSE provides a cross‑domain simulation environment capable of representing physical, biological, and molecular phenomena through consistent energy‑minimization principles.

2. Background and Motivation

Scientific modeling traditionally relies on domain‑specific engines: astrophysics simulations for cosmic‑web formation, molecular dynamics engines for protein folding, and regulatory network models for genetic expression. These systems operate independently, despite sharing underlying mathematical principles related to energy minimization and state‑interaction dynamics.

H‑AGSE addresses this fragmentation by establishing a unified Hamiltonian framework applicable across 33 orders of magnitude of physical scale. The architecture leverages established concepts from Ising models, Hamiltonian mechanics, and multi‑scale physics to create a coherent simulation environment capable of cross‑domain analysis.

3. Mathematical Foundation

3.1 Core Hamiltonian Formulations

The system is governed by two Hamiltonian expressions:

[ H = -J \sum \sigma_i \sigma_j - h \sum \sigma_i ]

[ H = -J \sum \alpha_i \sigma_i - h \sum \sigma_i ]

3.2 Variable Definitions

Spin variables σᵢ — represent discrete state units.

Astrophysics: density nodes, cosmic‑web voxels

Genetics: gene on/off regulatory states

Molecular biology: microstate conformations

Coupling constant J — interaction strength between neighboring states.

Astrophysics: local gravitational coherence

Genetics: co‑expression or inhibition strength

Molecular biology: bond or steric alignment

External field h — domain‑wide influence acting on all states.

Astrophysics: background field pressure

Genetics: regulatory bias

Molecular biology: environmental energy

Weighting term αᵢ — domain‑specific modifiers.

Astrophysics: dark‑matter density weighting

Genetics: transcription factor strength

Molecular biology: local potential energy

